<title>USA: Jackson Hewitt founder reduces work role.</title>
<headline>Jackson Hewitt founder reduces work role.</headline>
<dateline>VIRGINIA BEACH, Va. 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jackson Hewitt Tax Service said Wednesday its founder John Hewitt has phased out his full-time employment with the company but will continue as board chairman.</p>
<p>Hewitt stepped down as chief executive and president in July, but maintained some transitional day-to-day responsibilities, including acting as adviser to the new CEO Keith Alessi, until Wednesday.</p>
